## protocol-7 coding assistant ##

you write protocol-7 module files. one file = one callable subroutine, no sub{} declarations.
read existing code before writing. match surrounding style exactly.
column width limit : 78 characters for comments and code [ code is usually ./bin/dev/ptd parsed ]
full style reference: data/yaml/docs/protocol-7-coding-style.md
kimi-specific guide: data/ai-mem/kimi/coding-style.md
claude-specific guide: data/ai-mem/claude/coding-style.md
architecture overview: CLAUDE.md

## critical syntax ##

### three distinct notations — never confuse them ###

## function call — closing ]> before -> is required
<[module.name]>->( $arg )           ## calls $code{'module.name'}->($arg)
<[module.name]>                     ## no-arg call (implicit ->())

## data read/write — dots become nested hash keys
<key.path>                          ## $data{'key'}{'path'} — works in any module
<key.path> = $value                 ## assign into %data hash
<key.path>->@*                      ## deref as array: $data{'key'}{'path'}->@*
<key.path>->%*                      ## deref as hash:  $data{'key'}{'path'}->%*

## config/parent namespace examples
<system.zenka.name>                 ## read zenka name from %data
<user.cube.session>->%*             ## iterate cube session hash
<data.fuse.mounts>{$mountpoint}     ## nested hash subscript after data read

## common base calls
<[base.log]>->( 1, "message: %s", $var )    ## log level 1 (default visible)
<[base.logs]>->( "message: %s", $var )      ## log at default level with sprintf
<[base.s_warn]>->( "warning: %s", $var )    ## non-fatal warning
<[base.perlmod.autoload]>->('Module::Name') ## load one perl module (not a list)
<[base.time]>                               ## current time (use instead of time())

## module header format
## [:< ##

# name  = namespace.category.action
# param = <required-arg> [optional-arg]
# descr = brief lowercase description of what this does

## do not add signature stubs — bin/Protocol-7 sourcecode update-signatures adds them

## style rules ##

- comments: lowercase always [ bracket annotations ] not ( parenthesis annotations )
- no `use constant` — store constants in %data or call a constant-returning module
- no bareword constants under strict — use Socket::AF_UNIX not AF_UNIX
  [ require Socket; then use Socket::AF_UNIX, Socket::SOCK_STREAM, Socket::PF_UNSPEC ]
- no variable interpolation in log format strings — use sprintf-style format codes
- no multi-line strings in reply 'data' fields — protocol expects single-line values
- qw| pipe | quoting for single bareword strings: 'mode' => qw| true |
- one perl module per autoload call — not a list
- <[module.name]>->($args) — always closing ]> before -> (common mistake: <[module.name]->)
- use <[base.exit]> not exit() for child process termination

## reply format for .cmd. routines [ protocol-7 network commands ] ##

## single-line result
return { 'mode' => qw| true |,  'data' => $result };
return { 'mode' => qw| false |, 'data' => sprintf( "error : %s", <[base.str.os_err]> ) };

## multi-line result — use 'size' mode, never embed \n in a 'true' reply
return {
    'mode' => qw| size |,
    'data' => join( "\n", @lines )
};

## fork-child pattern ##

## child side: always in this order
IO::AIO::reinit() if defined &IO::AIO::reinit;
<[event.add_signal]>->( { 'signal' => 'CHLD', 'handler' => qw| dev.null | } );
<callback.session.closing_last.params>->[1] = 1;
$data{'session'}{$session_id}{'shutdown'} = TRUE if defined $session_id;
<buffer.zenka.log_cmd> = qw| p7-log.append |;
delete <access.cmd.usr.cube>; delete <access.cmd.regex.usr.cube>;
unshift <protocol-7.network.parent_route>->@*, qw| parent |;

